hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1358","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami told us, and Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told us, and this is the hadith of Al-Mukhurami, he told us Ruh bin Ubadah, Shu’bah and Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah said regarding the fear prayer: “A group stands behind the imam and another group behind him, so he leads those behind him in one rak’ah.” and two prostrations, then he will sit in his place until they perform one rak’ah and two prostrations, then they will move to the place of their companions, then their companions will shift To the place of these people, and lead them in prayer one rak’ah and two prostrations, then he will sit in his place until they pray one rak’ah and two prostrations, then he will salute.”"
"1359","Secondly... they said, Ruh narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of Sahl bin Abu Hathamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something like this"
"1360","Al-Mukhurami narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi also narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of His father, like this, is what Al-Mukhurami told us about it, following the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim."
